diplomats from ukraine and russia are in  turkey this morning for a new round of  peace talks the kremlin says they may  start tomorrow fighting continued  through the weekend with russia focusing  most on capturing territory in eastern  ukraine including the devastated city of  mariupo deborah patta spoke to refugees  from that city she's in the capital kiev  where ukraine's president sent a message  to russia through the media deborah good  morning  good morning in an unusual interview  ukrainian president vladimir zelinsky  spoke to four prominent russian  journalists detailing the horrors of the  war being waged in his country the  kremlin of course promptly banned it but  it was broadcast outside the country now  given what we have seen on the ground it  is no wonder russia did not want it  aired there  plumes of black smoke choked the sky  after a russian cruise missile plowed  into a fuel depot in lev  firefighters battled for 12 hours to put  out the blaze  around kiev fighting and bombings have  intensified leaving behind  battle-scarred landscapes  but it's mario paul where apocalyptic  scenes show the real extent of the human  toll of this war  valentino was born in this house married  and had children there a lifetime of  memories reduced to rubble  what is left for us she sobs there's no  way to live here now  alexander also stayed and is just  grateful to be alive  i survived he says breaking down crying  as he sends a message to his daughter  thank god your dad is alive  she pains victoria mendinska remained in  mario paul for three weeks before  finally making the death-defying car  trip out of there escaping to the town  of bravery  the street where she lived now looks  like this it must have been terrifying  yes and i cried  because  it's  it's hard to speak  victoria's daughter masha remembers  everything  were you scared  her school was bombed her childhood  blown up  one year ago she celebrated her birthday  surrounded by laughter  i had so many friends she said and now i  have no friends  on sunday a very different celebration  masha turned seven no longer a carefree  school girl but one of the four million  children displaced by this war  a humanitarian corridor was opened up  briefly yesterday allowing the  evacuation of just over 500 people from  maripo but officials say they are still  over  fifty thousand trapped there and they  are running very low on food vlad  all right deborah pada and key for us  deborah thank you very much
 

